<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's NSW 1997/98 state budget table.</title>
<headline>Australia's NSW 1997/98 state budget table.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table details the budget projections of the Australian state of New South Wales contained in the 1997/98 (July/June) budget released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The budget, released by Treasurer Michael Egan, forecasts a A$27 million surplus for 1997/98.</p>
<p>		     1996/97     1997/98     1998/99    1999/2000</p>
<p>			A$ mln	A$ mln	A$ mln	A$ mln</p>
<p>Current Account</p>
<p>     Outlays	19,690	20,515	21,070	21,656</p>
<p>     Receipts     21,543	22,763	23,284	24,098</p>
<p>			------	------	------	------</p>
<p>     Surplus	 1,853	 2,247	 2,214	 2,442</p>
<p>Capital Account</p>
<p>     Outlays	 2,658	 3,301	 3,025	 3,117</p>
<p>     Receipts	  872	 1,081	   847	   870</p>
<p>			------	------	------	------</p>
<p>     (Deficit)    (1,786)     (2,220)     (2,178)     (2,247)</p>
<p>UNDERLYNG SURPLUS     67	    27	    36	    195</p>
<p>The underlying result excludes extraordinary items such as equity restructures and sale of government business enterprises.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
